<section class="section" data-reveal>
  <div class="container" style="text-align:center">
    <p class="section-label">What it is not</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Clear on scope</h2>
    <p class="section-subtitle" style="margin-bottom:24px">ASD is a <strong style="color:var(--text-primary)">code-level overlay</strong>. It's the layer agents query before they read, write, or refactor &mdash; not a linter, not a search tool.</p>
    <div style="display:flex;gap:24px;justify-content:center;flex-wrap:wrap;max-width:700px;margin:0 auto">
      <div style="flex:1;min-width:200px;background:var(--bg-secondary);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius-sm);padding:16px;text-align:left">
        <div style="font-size:12px;color:var(--text-muted);margin-bottom:6px;font-weight:600">NOT a linter</div>
        <div style="font-size:13px;color:var(--text-secondary)">Linters check style. ASD records <em>decisions</em> &mdash; why a function exists, what it's allowed to touch, who approved it.</div>
      </div>
      <div style="flex:1;min-width:200px;background:var(--bg-secondary);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius-sm);padding:16px;text-align:left">
        <div style="font-size:12px;color:var(--text-muted);margin-bottom:6px;font-weight:600">NOT a code-search tool</div>
        <div style="font-size:13px;color:var(--text-secondary)">grep finds strings. ASD answers <em>what does this touch, who decided this, was it approved.</em></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" data-reveal>
  <div class="container" style="max-width:760px;margin:0 auto">
    <p class="section-label">License</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Why BSL 1.1?</h2>
    <p style="font-size:16px;color:var(--text-secondary);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:24px;text-align:center">AgentStateDeveloper is built to become infrastructure for agent-driven coding. Infrastructure primitives are strip-mining targets: cloud providers offer them as managed services, capture the value, and contribute nothing back. BSL 1.1 closes that gap.</p>

    <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:12px;margin-bottom:28px">
      <div style="display:flex;gap:12px;align-items:flex-start;padding:12px 16px;background:var(--bg-secondary);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius-sm)">
        <span style="color:var(--success);font-weight:700;font-size:18px;flex-shrink:0">&#10003;</span>
        <span style="font-size:14px;color:var(--text-secondary);line-height:1.6"><strong style="color:var(--text-primary)">Individuals, startups, and enterprises</strong> using ASD internally &mdash; including in production &mdash; are unaffected.</span>
      </div>
      <div style="display:flex;gap:12px;align-items:flex-start;padding:12px 16px;background:var(--bg-secondary);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius-sm)">
        <span style="color:var(--warning);font-weight:700;font-size:18px;flex-shrink:0">&#9888;</span>
        <span style="font-size:14px;color:var(--text-secondary);line-height:1.6">The restriction covers <strong style="color:var(--text-primary)">one specific case</strong>: offering ASD as a hosted or managed service to third parties without a commercial agreement.</span>
      </div>
      <div style="display:flex;gap:12px;align-items:flex-start;padding:12px 16px;background:var(--bg-secondary);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius-sm)">
        <span style="color:var(--accent);font-weight:700;font-size:18px;flex-shrink:0">&#8634;</span>
        <span style="font-size:14px;color:var(--text-secondary);line-height:1.6">After <strong style="color:var(--text-primary)">four years</strong>, each version converts to <strong style="color:var(--text-primary)">Apache 2.0 permanently</strong>, with no conditions.</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" data-reveal>
  <div class="container" style="text-align:center">
    <p class="section-label">Part of a suite</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Pairs with CTXone &amp; AgentStateGraph</h2>
    <p class="section-subtitle">ASD is per-developer <strong>code context</strong>. <a href="https://ctxone.com" target="_blank">CTXone</a> is the <strong>team layer</strong> &mdash; shared decisions, plans, and memory that travel across the whole team; installing either offers to set up the other. <a href="https://agentstategraph.dev" target="_blank">AgentStateGraph</a> is the underlying state substrate. Together they give agents accountable state across code, team, and runtime.</p>
    <p class="section-subtitle" style="margin-bottom:24px">ASD ships in three editions: <strong>OSS</strong> (this repo &mdash; the full per-developer engine), <strong>Team</strong> (the cross-repo layer, paired with CTXone), and <strong>Enterprise</strong> (org-scale governance: endpoint registry, change-governance gates, audit/SIEM export, RBAC).</p>
    <a class="btn btn-primary" href="https://ctxone.com" target="_blank">Visit ctxone.com</a>
